@startuml components
title M-UM1: component view within privileged process boundaries (unimplemented design)
left to right direction

actor "Configured caller\ninstaller / dispatcher / operator UID" as Caller
component "sudo\ntrusted root transition; exact path, no args" as Sudo
package "swarma-user-manager process\nroot; one helper-op/1 invocation (v0)" {
  component "Sudo entry validation\neffective UID + SUDO_UID + argv" as MEntry
  component "Closed helper decoder\n16 KiB / 5 s" as MDecode
  component "Caller policy\nrole / ownership / quota" as MPolicy
  component "Lock, journal and recovery\ndependency recovery / bounded retire batches" as Recovery
  component "OS account backend\nmacOS dscl / Linux groupadd, useradd" as Accounts
  component "Descriptor-safe file operations\ntrusted directory descriptors; no-follow" as Files
  component "Retirement / metadata sweep\nquiescence; keys destroyed before deletion\nclosed-schema service-generated export only" as Archive
  component "Egress adapter (v1)\npf / nftables; evidence matrix" as Firewall
  component "Read-only effect.observe\noriginal caller / operator; six evidence states" as Observe
  component "Authorised exec.stop\nreceipt + live identity; TERM / KILL\naccount-wide absence ONLY; latest-receipt fence" as Stop
}
package "swarma-user-launcher process\nroot until privilege drop; one launch-op/1 invocation (v0)" {
  component "Sudo entry + closed decoder\n80 KiB / 5 s" as LEntry
  component "Launch validation\ncaller / generation / executor / home" as Launch
  component "Descriptor-safe executable / home opens\nno-follow; type / owner checks" as LFiles
  component "Receipt writer\natomic write before GID/UID drop" as Receipt
  component "R-FD3 descriptor lifecycle\nbounded immutable FD3; receipt/drop/exec ordering" as Exec
}
database "Root-owned configuration\nroles, ranges, metadata retention, approved digests\nInstaller places it (§11)" as Config
database "Root-owned manager control state\nledger + allocation cursor; lock; journal; audit\nlauncher-written start receipts; v1 applied state" as State
database "OS directory service\naccount / primary-group records\nmanager-created; backend storage" as OS
folder "Account-owned homes\nroot-controlled home roots\nRoot quarantine + metadata exports" as Homes
component "Kernel egress rules (v1)\nhelper-owned pf anchor / nftables table" as Kernel
component "curator-run -> harness\nagent account UID; immutable plan only" as Agent
component "swarma-credential-broker\nservice account; owns credentials / bindings / leases" as Broker
component "Profile proxy (v1)\ntrusted service account; verified listener" as Proxy

Caller --> Sudo : operation JSON on stdin
Sudo --> MEntry
Sudo --> LEntry : configured dispatcher ONLY
MEntry --> MDecode
MDecode --> MPolicy
MPolicy --> Config
MPolicy --> Recovery
Recovery --> State : shared transition lock; journal before actions; bounded batches yield
Recovery --> Accounts
Recovery --> Archive
Recovery --> Firewall
Recovery --> Stop
Recovery --> Observe
Observe --> State : journal-serialized evidence; no new mutation
Accounts --> OS
Accounts --> Files
Archive --> Files
Files --> Homes
Firewall --> Kernel
Firewall --> Proxy : verify owner/generation AND served digest; no shared lock across query
Firewall --> State : publish applied state after successful apply
Stop --> State : matching root start receipt
Stop --> Agent : latest receipt/current generation; TERM/KILL same UID set; quiet absence
LEntry --> Launch
Launch --> Config
Launch --> State : same transition lock + bounded dependency recovery; active owned generation
Launch --> LFiles : no-follow executable / home
LFiles --> Homes : opened home as cwd
Launch --> Receipt
Receipt --> State
Receipt --> Exec
Exec --> Agent : verified exec; only standard FDs + FD3 plan
Agent --> Broker : fresh connection; lease
Broker --> State : reads ledger / v1 applied state; readability is not authority

note bottom of Recovery
  Refusal: invalid invocation/schema, role, ownership, quota, unmanaged objects,
  request_id conflict, unsafe path (§§2-6). Terminal same effect replays recorded
  result plus current state; admitted stop/retire pending continues same effect.
  Recovery validates shared integrity/accounting, then dependencies, not all retirements.
  Bounded cleanup batches yield lock; reservations/fences remain until full cleanup.
  R-LOCK: no synchronous platform-service call under state lock; per-record in-flight marker.
end note
note bottom of Launch
  Refusal: inactive/wrong-owner generation, unapproved executor, digest mismatch,
  existing execution receipt, failed privilege drop (§7).
  Resolve ambiguous launch through same effect/receipt; never a second start (§§4.6, 7).
  Retain generation lock through receipt and verified UID/GID drop; executable handle through exec.
  Scrub untrusted inherited FDs first; close internal handles at last use / qualified close-on-exec;
  release on every failure. Executor receives only 0-2 and read-only immutable FD3 (R-FD3).
  Dispatcher alone invokes launcher; host requests host_start from dispatcher.
  I4 joint admission/permit/fence publication remains gated (§14 question 3).
end note
note bottom of Stop
  TERM/KILL and verification cover every current-generation UID process, including escaped/OS starts.
  Latest receipt fence on every continuation; terminal stop replay never signals.
  No harness native-lock attestation (§4.7).
  Session-host recovery: fresh agent-UID runner checks native lock under closed fence;
  unknown result keeps parked (session-host §3.5).
end note
note bottom of Archive
  Destroy declared keys before home deletion; failure/unknown keeps retiring (§4.4.1).
  Delete all home content/names/links through descriptors; no classification.
  Export only closed-schema service-generated metadata; no agent-controlled strings/names/links/bodies.
  Export schema/provenance/naming/bounds and audit encoding open (§14 question 6).
  Separate operator retention: confidentiality not guaranteed; format unpublished (§14 question 1).
end note
note bottom of Observe
  recorded + current state; pending; rolled_back; not_recorded; unavailable; contradictory (R-OBS).
  Only complete authoritative evidence proves not_recorded; expiry/read failure -> unavailable.
  Original principal may observe after mutation-grant expiry; no new effect is authorised.
  Evidence retained until permanent inadmissibility; exact bounds/coverage open (§14 question 8).
end note
note bottom of Firewall
  R-NETBIND: root-owned binding beside user-manager.json; dispatcher pins at prepare.
  Verify served digest; re-apply existing allocations flushes kernel/old proxy sessions.
  R-SVC-EGRESS: dispatcher/host deny-all, broker via own proxy; resolver sandbox qualified.
  Installer owns start-time and periodic service-policy checks; lapse drops readiness.
  R-WORKPLACE: helper v1 enforced activation incl. loopback; rb-exec under service UID.
  v1: refuse unsupported tuple; never report enforcement without whole-matrix evidence.
  Denial before first launch; retain until account/group removal (§8).
end note
note "Defining spec: [[../spec/helper.md#1-purpose §1 process split]], [[../spec/helper.md#2-invocation §§2-3 invocation/policy]],\n[[../spec/helper.md#46-lock-journal-and-idempotency §4.6 recovery]], [[../spec/helper.md#6-file-operations §6 paths]],\n[[../spec/helper.md#7-the-launcher-swarma-user-launcher §7 launcher]], [[../spec/helper.md#8-firewall-per-account-v1 §8 egress]].\nBoxes are conceptual responsibilities within binaries, not implemented classes or extra processes.\nCurrent: nothing implemented; v0 accounts/launcher, v1 egress, v2 grants (§13).\nv0/v1 refuse grants; v2 subject-bound chain checks target/time/revocation (§9); signature grammar open.\nSH2+ joint admission remains gated by I4 publication (§§7, 14); dispatcher alone invokes the launcher.\nDonor provisioning is a separate component; variant B disabled pending its spec (§1.1)." as Scope
Scope .. MEntry
note bottom of State
  R-GEN: fresh random 128-bit generations, ledger store epoch and reader floors.
  External restore mark closes every consumer before restored bytes; surviving evidence reconciled.
  No retirement resurrection; lost coverage unavailable, never not_recorded (§4.6.1).
  R-FATE process table at §7: selected kill domains / affected sets qualify before activation.
  Every supervisor write checks durable daemon-instance epoch; no live adoption.
end note
@enduml
